  {%- comment -%}
    Guard against third-party stylesheets that reset <em> globally.

    This theme repurposes italic as its highlight control: authors mark a word italic in the
    rich text editor and snippets/highlighted-text.liquid rewrites <em> into
    <em class="highlighted-text ... not-italic"> so it renders upright in the highlight colour,
    never in italic letterforms.

    The Wigzo exit-intent app injects app.wigzo.com/assets/plugins/exitintent/exitintent.css at
    runtime, and that file carries a single unscoped declaration:

        em { font-style: italic !important }

    Being !important it outranks the theme's .not-italic utility — and inline styles too — so
    every highlighted word on the storefront rendered italic. It is absent from the theme editor
    because app scripts do not run there, which is why the two previews disagreed.

    .highlighted-text is (0,1,0) against that rule's (0,0,1), so among !important declarations
    this wins on specificity and load order is irrelevant — it holds even though the app injects
    its stylesheet after ours. Kept inline and render-blocking so highlighted words never flash
    italic before an external file arrives, and scoped to the highlight element alone so genuine
    italics elsewhere are untouched.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <style>.highlighted-text{font-style:normal!important}</style>

