  {%- comment -%}
    CHECKOUT ROUTING — the whole of it.

    Magic Checkout is a purely client-side interceptor: magic-shopify.js adds
    one delegated click listener on `document`, matches [name="checkout"], and
    calls stopImmediatePropagation(). It never rewrites the cart form. So not
    rendering it is a complete, clean opt-out — the theme's two checkout
    buttons (sections/main-cart.liquid:595 and sections/cart-drawer.liquid:698)
    then submit POST /cart normally and Shopify serves native checkout. The
    sticky buy bar inherits this for free, because it works by clicking the
    real [name="checkout"] button rather than navigating to /checkout
    (snippets/sleek-quick-add-modal.liquid:935-948).

    Gated on the display currency, not on the country, so the merchant's rule
    holds exactly: native checkout only while USD prices are on screen. If the
    USD toggle is switched off, or the rate is set to 0, a US shopper is shown
    INR and correctly falls back to Magic Checkout — a country test would have
    sent them to native checkout with INR prices and no COD.

    Gated here in theme.liquid rather than inside the snippet: Razorpay's app
    owns snippets/razorpay-magic-checkout.liquid and can overwrite it on an app
    update or a theme republish. This file is ours. Re-check after any Razorpay
    app update.
  {%- endcomment -%}
